    <briefdescription>
<para>Stateless search engine for structured log entries. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1observability_1_1_log_search_engine" kindref="compound">LogSearchEngine</ref> operates purely in-memory on a snapshot of entries provided by the caller. Typical usage is to pass agg.entries() where agg is a <ref refid="classthemis_1_1observability_1_1_log_aggregator" kindref="compound">LogAggregator</ref> instance.</para>
<para>Thread safety: <ref refid="classthemis_1_1observability_1_1_log_search_engine" kindref="compound">LogSearchEngine</ref> itself holds no mutable state; all state lives in the <ref refid="structthemis_1_1observability_1_1_log_search_query" kindref="compound">LogSearchQuery</ref> and the input vector. It is therefore safe to call <ref refid="classthemis_1_1observability_1_1_log_search_engine_1af6103a2dee0f5d1b33c5ea93e6dfe960" kindref="member">search()</ref> concurrently from multiple threads on the same engine instance without additional synchronisation. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
